+** OvVec: accumulate WAL frames and hand the whole run to the VFS at once.
+**
+** Frames are appended at strictly ascending, contiguous offsets, so a commit
+** is one contiguous region of the log written as two calls per page: one for
+** the 24-byte frame header and one for the page image.  Collecting them and
+** issuing a single scatter/gather write costs one syscall per batch instead
+** of two per page, and needs no contiguity test because the layout of the log
+** guarantees it.  The bytes written are unchanged, so the resulting WAL is
+** identical to one written frame by frame.
